WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:01.835
-Hello, everybody.

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:03.102
Welcome back
to our temporary studio

00:00:03.102 --> 00:00:04.403
in the captain's quarters.

00:00:04.403 --> 00:00:06.406
You know, we've been going
through our viewer mail,

00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:07.606
and while many of you think

00:00:07.606 --> 00:00:09.709
the new maritime-themed set
is great,

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:13.212
some of you most certainly
do not-ical.

00:00:13.212 --> 00:00:15.682
Oof.
I told you that joke stunk.

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:17.717
-Arr! Thanks for trying it.

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:19.152
-And since I did, can we maybe

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:20.720
keep the interruptions
to a minimum?

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:21.688
-Okay.

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:23.088
-Speaking of half-assed efforts,

00:00:23.088 --> 00:00:24.824
the president is trying
to convince Americans

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:26.425
he suddenly cares
about the pandemic

00:00:26.425 --> 00:00:27.793
he's been ignoring for months

00:00:27.793 --> 00:00:30.296
as he also threatens
to send more secret police

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:31.697
to cities across the country.

00:00:31.697 --> 00:00:34.734
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:39.572
Donald Trump is
trailing Joe Biden

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:41.974
by as much as 15 points
in the latest polls.

00:00:41.974 --> 00:00:44.744
He is as unpopular as any
president in modern history,

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:46.646
and he's facing a larger deficit

00:00:46.646 --> 00:00:48.681
than any incumbent
has ever overcome

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:50.016
at this point in the campaign.

00:00:50.016 --> 00:00:53.619
But as we all know, Donald Trump
is a master tactician

00:00:53.619 --> 00:00:55.154
and a marketing genius.

00:00:55.154 --> 00:00:58.024
It was only a matter of time
before he cooked up

00:00:58.024 --> 00:01:00.460
a foolproof plan
to win back those voters.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.762
And on Tuesday,
with the nation's eyes upon him

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:04.364
at a televised press briefing,

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:07.500
he finally deployed
his latest master stroke.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.002
-President Trump was asked
late today

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:11.270
about Jeffrey Epstein's
alleged co-conspirator,

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:12.438
Ghislaine Maxwell.

00:01:12.438 --> 00:01:13.573
She pleaded not guilty

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:15.441
to sex-trafficking charges
last week,

00:01:15.441 --> 00:01:17.209
one of her alleged victims
describing her

00:01:17.209 --> 00:01:19.011
as a predator and monster.

00:01:19.011 --> 00:01:21.580
The president today saying
he hasn't followed her case,

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:24.617
that they've met numerous times,
and that he wishes her well.

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:26.919
-I just wish her well, frankly.

00:01:26.919 --> 00:01:28.854
I've met her numerous times
over the years,

00:01:28.854 --> 00:01:30.790
especially since I lived
in Palm Beach,

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:33.292
and I guess they lived
in Palm Beach,

00:01:33.292 --> 00:01:34.693
but I wish her well.

00:01:34.693 --> 00:01:36.362
-Checkmate, Joe Biden!

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:38.831
Just like the Trump team
drew it up on the chalkboard.

00:01:38.831 --> 00:01:39.999
In front of millions
of Americans,

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:41.801
the president publicly
sent well wishes

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:43.503
to an alleged sex trafficker

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:46.306
while reminding everyone he's
been friends with her for years.

00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:49.576
I mean, you just can't teach
that kind of political talent.

00:01:49.576 --> 00:01:51.010
Now all Trump has to do
is sit back

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:52.511
and watch the votes roll in.

00:01:52.511 --> 00:01:56.282
Now, I know you Monday-morning
quarterbacks out there

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:58.751
might think that publicly
sending well wishes

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:00.186
to Jeffrey Epstein's wing-woman

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:02.254
100 days before
a presidential election is,

00:02:02.254 --> 00:02:04.023
shall we say, a misstep.

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:06.492
But, you see, Trump is always
10 steps ahead.

00:02:06.492 --> 00:02:08.294
When you go left, he goes right.

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:10.430
When you zig, he says
nice things about someone

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:12.031
who was recently apprehended
by federal agents

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:13.432
while hiding out
in a remote compound.

00:02:13.432 --> 00:02:15.601
Because if there is one thing

00:02:15.601 --> 00:02:17.904
that Trump's base
cares most about,

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:21.374
it's a woman whose first name
sounds like a French perfume

00:02:21.374 --> 00:02:23.242
for someone who is
keeping a secret.

00:02:23.242 --> 00:02:25.645
Ghislaine. Shh!

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:28.380
And again, one day we will
get a second close-up camera

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:29.782
for right over there.

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:32.251
My favorite thing about this
is imagining the staff reaction.

00:02:32.251 --> 00:02:34.254
They only called
this press conference

00:02:34.254 --> 00:02:35.955
to try to improve
Trump's poll numbers.

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:38.557
You know they must have tried
so hard to keep him on script.

00:02:38.557 --> 00:02:40.760
"Mr. President, we just need you
to focus on the facts

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.061
of the coronavirus
and only the facts."

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:43.229
"Uh-huh."

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:44.430
"So just, you know,
stick to the script."

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:45.598
"Got it."

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:46.599
"All you have to do
is sound presidential,

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:47.767
and the media will eat it up."

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:48.935
"Don't worry.
I won't let you down.

00:02:48.935 --> 00:02:50.403
Just one question --
should I remind people

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:52.038
that I partied with Epstein?

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:53.372
Is that a good idea
or a great idea?

00:02:53.372 --> 00:02:55.408
I think it might be
a great idea."

00:02:55.408 --> 00:02:56.976
And yet despite
this insane tangent,

00:02:56.976 --> 00:02:58.977
the media still fell
for Trump's act,

00:02:58.977 --> 00:03:01.847
simply because his team dosed
his Diet Coke with NyQuil

00:03:01.847 --> 00:03:03.215
and got him to read
a prepared statement

00:03:03.215 --> 00:03:05.250
pretending to take
the crisis seriously.

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:07.587
Before the briefing, ABC wrote,

00:03:07.587 --> 00:03:09.822
"The president is displaying
a new tone

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:11.357
and a new level of engagement."

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:13.592
CNN called it
a "relatively sober tone."

00:03:13.592 --> 00:03:16.428
And Bloomberg said,
"Trump reboots virus briefings

00:03:16.428 --> 00:03:18.664
with warning
and a shift in tone."

00:03:18.664 --> 00:03:20.266
Good Lord, I really think

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:23.903
you could duct-tape a spatula
to a golden retriever's paw,

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:28.474
and half of the media would say,
"Oh, my God, that dog's a chef."

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:29.675
What's wrong with you guys?

00:03:29.675 --> 00:03:31.243
How can you keep
falling for this?

00:03:31.243 --> 00:03:32.711
It's been five years
of this B.S.,

00:03:32.711 --> 00:03:35.180
and still, every time
President Werewolf over here

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:37.583
manages to novocaine his way
through a prepared statement

00:03:37.583 --> 00:03:39.719
without passing out
at the podium, you act like

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:41.587
he's a totally different person
all of a sudden.

00:03:41.587 --> 00:03:43.956
You know,
I say President Werewolf,

00:03:43.956 --> 00:03:46.125
but really, he's more like
a reverse werewolf.

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:48.328
He terrorizes townspeople
all the time,

00:03:48.328 --> 00:03:50.229
and then he's normal
for a couple of hours

00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:51.430
when there's a full moon.

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:54.701
"I owe you all an apology
for the past 30 days.

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:58.604
My behavior has been monstrous."

00:03:58.604 --> 00:04:00.039
Look, 74-year-olds don't change

00:04:00.039 --> 00:04:01.740
unless they're characters
in a Clint Eastwood movie

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:03.776
where a bunch of retired
bank robbers go to outer space,

00:04:03.776 --> 00:04:05.811
even though all they ever
really learn is how to have

00:04:05.811 --> 00:04:08.648
a slightly better relationship
with their estranged daughter,

00:04:08.648 --> 00:04:10.316
let's say Laura Linney.

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:12.484
"You were never there for me."

00:04:12.484 --> 00:04:14.820
"Those bank robberies paid
for your fancy college."

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:17.690
"I didn't want a fancy college.
I wanted a father."

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:21.694
"I need to go now, Becky.
We're robbing Mars."

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:24.130
Look, you know Trump's just
going to steal his phone back

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:25.732
and tweet some racist nonsense,
right?

00:04:25.732 --> 00:04:27.900
He repeatedly used a racist term

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.301
for the coronavirus
in the briefing.

00:04:29.301 --> 00:04:30.970
You don't even need to wait
until he tweets.

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:33.940
He morphed back into the real
Trump mid-press conference.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:37.610
Just compare his supposed tone
change from his scripted remarks

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:40.613
to an off-the-cuff comment
he made just minutes later.

00:04:40.613 --> 00:04:42.682
-It will probably,
unfortunately,

00:04:42.682 --> 00:04:44.416
get worse before it gets better.

00:04:44.416 --> 00:04:47.520
The virus will disappear.
It will disappear.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:50.322
-My God, I'd say he suffers from
extreme short-term memory loss.

00:04:50.322 --> 00:04:52.425
But then again,
he aced that cognitive test.

00:04:52.425 --> 00:04:53.693
So what do I know?

00:04:53.693 --> 00:04:55.127
It's too bad
coronavirus can't be cured

00:04:55.127 --> 00:04:57.229
by correctly identifying
an elephant on a piece of paper.

00:04:57.229 --> 00:04:59.498
Then Trump would have knocked
that [bleep] out of the park.

00:04:59.498 --> 00:05:00.867
Of course,
the idea that the virus

00:05:00.867 --> 00:05:02.869
will just magically disappear
is deranged.

00:05:02.869 --> 00:05:05.104
And since the very beginning
of his political career,

00:05:05.104 --> 00:05:06.138
we've known that both Trump

00:05:06.138 --> 00:05:07.473
and the political movement
he leads

00:05:07.473 --> 00:05:10.343
are deeply, deeply detached
from reality.

00:05:10.343 --> 00:05:13.979
Sometimes that manifests itself
in small but bizarre ways,

00:05:13.979 --> 00:05:16.916
like when he drew with a Sharpie
on a hurricane map

00:05:16.916 --> 00:05:19.117
or claimed God
stopped it from raining

00:05:19.117 --> 00:05:21.187
at his inauguration,
even though people in the crowd

00:05:21.187 --> 00:05:23.222
were literally
holding umbrellas.

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:24.423
This guy lies about the weather

00:05:24.423 --> 00:05:26.224
more than your local
meteorologist.

00:05:26.224 --> 00:05:28.160
You told me we were gonna
have clear skies all weekend,

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:30.463
and then I end up
wearing a poncho to the beach.

00:05:30.463 --> 00:05:33.265
Ugh. The last time I listen
to Thunder Rains.

00:05:33.265 --> 00:05:36.335
And it's important to say,
this isn't unique to Trump.

00:05:36.335 --> 00:05:38.971
The modern conservative movement
is a paranoid movement

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:40.406
obsessed
with conspiracy theories.

00:05:40.406 --> 00:05:43.075
Remember, this is the same
political movement

00:05:43.075 --> 00:05:46.512
that thinks the world's
scientists all got together

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:48.414
and fabricated
the climate crisis

00:05:48.414 --> 00:05:51.383
as part of an elaborate plot to
outlaw airplanes and barbecues.

00:05:51.383 --> 00:05:53.252
Good thing we elected
Donald Trump

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:55.088
to protect our flights
and social gatherings.

00:05:55.088 --> 00:05:56.856
And now those same lunatics

00:05:56.856 --> 00:05:59.024
think graffiti
and light property damage

00:05:59.024 --> 00:06:00.426
constitute domestic terrorism.

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:01.560
For example, take acting

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:03.696
Secretary of Homeland Security
Chad Wolf.

00:06:03.696 --> 00:06:07.266
You know, Drakkar Noir,
if it grew up to be a real boy.

00:06:07.266 --> 00:06:09.802
Pretty sure this dude
had a minor role on "Entourage"

00:06:09.802 --> 00:06:11.503
as a personal trainer
who's friends with turtle.

00:06:11.503 --> 00:06:14.173
He looks like a guy
who on a first date

00:06:14.173 --> 00:06:15.841
would tell you he was a commando

00:06:15.841 --> 00:06:18.277
in a top secret army unit
called the Omega Squad.

00:06:18.277 --> 00:06:20.412
And then you'd get home
and Google it

00:06:20.412 --> 00:06:21.748
and find out Omega Squad

00:06:21.748 --> 00:06:23.616
is a paintball range
two towns over.

00:06:23.616 --> 00:06:26.518
Wolf put out a statement on
the administration's decision

00:06:26.518 --> 00:06:27.853
to send secret police
to Portland

00:06:27.853 --> 00:06:29.889
to snatch protesters
off the street

00:06:29.889 --> 00:06:32.391
and stuff them in unmarked vans,

00:06:32.391 --> 00:06:35.594
in which DHS uses the phrases
"violent mob,"

00:06:35.594 --> 00:06:37.629
"violent criminals,"
or "violent anarchists"

00:06:37.629 --> 00:06:41.133
a total of 76 times.

00:06:41.133 --> 00:06:45.704
Is this a press statement or
a page from Rorschach's journal?

00:06:45.704 --> 00:06:48.241
13-year-old, he's pretty psyched
about that joke.

00:06:48.241 --> 00:06:49.742
It's bad enough
to sound like a fascist,

00:06:49.742 --> 00:06:51.177
but at least crack open
a thesaurus.

00:06:51.177 --> 00:06:52.345
The only time it's permissible

00:06:52.345 --> 00:06:54.646
to use the phrase
"violent anarchy" that often

00:06:54.646 --> 00:06:57.182
is when you're reviewing
the music of Stomp.

00:06:57.182 --> 00:07:00.353
Guys, do we need
that many trash cans?"

00:07:00.353 --> 00:07:03.922
Maybe one of you
could learn guitar?

00:07:03.922 --> 00:07:05.891
Any time a government is calling
its own citizens

00:07:05.891 --> 00:07:08.360
violent anarchists
should raise alarms.

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:10.695
So what did these supposedly
violent anarchists do

00:07:10.695 --> 00:07:11.764
to deserve that name?

00:07:11.764 --> 00:07:14.132
Well, you'll be shocked
to find out.

00:07:14.132 --> 00:07:15.768
It's complete bull[bleep]

00:07:15.768 --> 00:07:19.772
-Chad Wolf, he is the acting
Secretary of Homeland Security.

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:22.107
To justify
what Donald Trump is doing.

00:07:22.107 --> 00:07:26.045
He tweeted out images of himself
viewing graffiti

00:07:26.045 --> 00:07:28.647
that had been put
on buildings in Portland.

00:07:28.647 --> 00:07:31.484
The DHS put out a statement
pointing to the buildings

00:07:31.484 --> 00:07:35.254
it said had been graffitied
by "violent anarchists."

00:07:35.254 --> 00:07:37.556
So the mission of the
Department of Homeland Security

00:07:37.556 --> 00:07:38.924
is to deploy secret police

00:07:38.924 --> 00:07:40.259
to the streets
of an American city

00:07:40.259 --> 00:07:45.163
to stop graffiti and some
light property damage.

00:07:45.163 --> 00:07:46.732
-Graffiti.

00:07:46.732 --> 00:07:49.535
You're going full dictator
over some graffiti.

00:07:49.535 --> 00:07:51.637
What's next, you gonna
send in SEAL Team Six

00:07:51.637 --> 00:07:52.872
to arrest lovestruck teens

00:07:52.872 --> 00:07:54.539
carving their initials
in a tree?

00:07:54.539 --> 00:07:57.210
"Okay, he just finished carving
the heart shape into the tree.

00:07:57.210 --> 00:07:58.544
Now he's going for the TLA."

00:07:58.544 --> 00:08:01.747
"Take the shot.
Take the shot, Todd!"

00:08:01.747 --> 00:08:04.116
That's right,
our government used graffiti

00:08:04.116 --> 00:08:06.519
to justify sending secret police
to an American city

00:08:06.519 --> 00:08:09.421
to abduct protesters
into unmarked vans

00:08:09.421 --> 00:08:10.856
without telling them
who they are,

00:08:10.856 --> 00:08:13.592
where they're going,
or why they've been arrested.

00:08:13.592 --> 00:08:15.360
But it would be bad enough
if what they were doing

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:18.397
was using secret police to
enforce laws against graffiti.

00:08:18.397 --> 00:08:19.565
That's already chilling.

00:08:19.565 --> 00:08:21.868
What they're actually doing
is even worse.

00:08:21.868 --> 00:08:25.203
They're just snatching peaceful
protesters off the street.

00:08:25.203 --> 00:08:26.772
They're kidnapping people

00:08:26.772 --> 00:08:29.508
and not even telling them
what they're being charged with.

00:08:29.508 --> 00:08:31.076
-Federal law enforcement
officers

00:08:31.076 --> 00:08:32.677
have been using
unmarked vehicles

00:08:32.677 --> 00:08:34.746
to drive around
downtown Portland

00:08:34.746 --> 00:08:37.850
and detain protesters
since at least Tuesday.

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:41.020
Personal accounts and multiple
videos posted online

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:43.789
show the officers
driving up to people,

00:08:43.789 --> 00:08:46.291
detaining individuals
with no explanation

00:08:46.291 --> 00:08:49.661
about why they're being
arrested, and driving off.

00:08:49.661 --> 00:08:51.863
-One came from a 29-year-old
named Mark Pettibone,

00:08:51.863 --> 00:08:53.065
who said that when
he was abducted,

00:08:53.065 --> 00:08:56.302
he did not know
if the men were even police.

00:08:56.302 --> 00:08:57.937
He thought they might be
far-right extremists.

00:08:57.937 --> 00:09:00.405
"I was terrified,"
he told "The Washington Post."

00:09:00.405 --> 00:09:02.375
"It seemed like
it was out of a horror/sci-fi,

00:09:02.375 --> 00:09:03.775
like a Philip K. Dick novel.

00:09:03.775 --> 00:09:05.377
It was like being preyed upon."

00:09:05.377 --> 00:09:07.579
-Leave it to Portland to use
a literary reference.

00:09:07.579 --> 00:09:08.981
If this happened anywhere else,

00:09:08.981 --> 00:09:10.749
people would say it seemed
like something out of a movie

00:09:10.749 --> 00:09:12.351
or at best a YA novel.

00:09:12.351 --> 00:09:15.020
But in Portland, you get, "It's
like a Philip K. Dick novel,

00:09:15.020 --> 00:09:16.689
less in sitting
but more in tenor,

00:09:16.689 --> 00:09:18.123
the later works, of course."

00:09:18.123 --> 00:09:21.026
And in case you're not a
Philip K. Dick fan, that's bad.

00:09:21.026 --> 00:09:23.295
The dude wrote
dystopian science fiction.

00:09:23.295 --> 00:09:24.997
None of it was ever good.

00:09:24.997 --> 00:09:26.398
He never wrote a novel called

00:09:26.398 --> 00:09:28.668
"Robots Took Over
and Gave Us Candy."

00:09:28.668 --> 00:09:30.236
When a secret paramilitary force

00:09:30.236 --> 00:09:32.471
is abducting peaceful protesters
in the dark of night

00:09:32.471 --> 00:09:33.739
without identifying themselves,

00:09:33.739 --> 00:09:36.108
that means even they know
what they're doing

00:09:36.108 --> 00:09:37.576
is a flagrant abuse of power.

00:09:37.576 --> 00:09:39.878
And you can tell
it's a flagrant abuse of power

00:09:39.878 --> 00:09:42.581
because they're using shady
and irregular tactics to do it.

00:09:42.581 --> 00:09:44.616
For example, federal officers

00:09:44.616 --> 00:09:47.319
appear to be using rental cars
from Enterprise

00:09:47.319 --> 00:09:48.754
